From b4080d300253aec8a61626fe9f595a72cc2c8a22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:54:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: register the rank-7 ROCmFP4 MMVQ mechanism,
 default-OFF and all

Registered although it ships OFF. The President's capability law makes a
capability droppable only when it is BROKEN, never when it is merely gated or
inert here, and default-OFF describes the shipped default rather than the
existence of the mechanism - the same reading the CHECKER-R3 R3-5 rows applied
to bf0abf0be. An unregistered mechanism is one an upstream bump can overwrite
without anything refusing, which is exactly the state the manifest exists to
prevent, and a gated win is the easiest kind to lose that way.

The entry records what is NOT established as prominently as what is: n=5 has
never executed in served generation, and the lane-206 op gate's finding that
MMVQ sits closer to the CPU reference than the f32 shader is partly structural,
because this type's CPU vec_dot_type is GGML_TYPE_Q8_0 - so it must not be
quoted as accuracy by whoever clears the default.

The quality_gate field is written so the next operator can re-run it verbatim,
including the two controls that make it readable at all: the ON-vs-OFF width
differential that proves MMVQ dispatched, and the ON-vs-ON serve control that
makes a text difference attributable.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Measured-effect: none - manifest registration only
---
 tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json b/tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json
index 4a646411e..e64e4f181 100644
--- a/tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json
+++ b/tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json
@@ -422,6 +422,22 @@
       "measured_effect": "NEUTRAL on gfx1103, and that is the whole claim. Op level: q6_k rows median ON/OFF 0.9796 against a control of 78 untouched op rows at 0.9990, p10-p90 [0.952, 1.053] - no q6_k row separates. Serve level TIED on all six prefill/decode cells at three prompt lengths. Output byte-identical, 1 sha256 per prompt over 12 arm-launches. NO SPEED WIN IS CLAIMED.",
       "valid_conditions": "Kept because it is strictly less work for a bit-identical result - one fewer workgroup barrier per row per superblock, and no shared-memory tile - on an engine that ships to other people's hardware, where LDS pressure and barrier cost are not what they are on a 780M. Protected as a NEUTRAL: an incoming upstream change that reverts it is not a regression to fight on speed grounds here, but it must be compared rather than silently taken, because the mechanism's value is off-seat.",
       "notes": "Also banks the falsification the next attempt needs: the per-row barrier was the leading mechanism for q6_k's reproducible ~35% mat-vec deficit on this box (41.0 GB/s against q5_k 63.8 and q4_k 72.5 at m=17408 n=3 k=5120). Removing it moves nothing. The deficit stands, unexplained."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "vulkan-rocmfp4-fast-q8_1-mmvq",
+      "status": "active",
+      "_registered": "2026-09-05, lane-206 integration (R8), once the disposition was decided. Registered although the mechanism ships DEFAULT OFF: the President's capability law makes a capability droppable only when BROKEN, never when it is merely gated, and default-OFF describes the shipped default rather than the existence of the mechanism (same reading as the CHECKER-R3 R3-5 rows).",
+      "mechanism": "ROCmFP4-FAST gets the integer-dot q8_1 MMVQ mat-vec pipelines it never had. The q8_1 selector (ggml_vk_get_dequantize_mul_mat_vec) already LISTED GGML_TYPE_Q4_0_ROCMFP4_FAST, but no pipeline was ever created for it, so quantize_y was computed true on every FP4 mat-vec, the selector returned null, and the dispatch fell back to the f32 dequant shader silently at every width. The port creates the pipelines and gates them to the widths where they win on this box: MMVQ at n=3 and n=5 only, f32 at n<=2, n=4 and n>5. Since lane-206 the whole route is additionally opt-in behind GGML_ARIFI_ROCMFP4_MMVQ=1.",
+      "commit": "f68a4bd25",
+      "also_commits": ["60f57787f", "ab04258bf", "294dfdbdd", "8e2acfd21", "ab1eeb108"],
+      "protected_paths": ["ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vecq_funcs.glsl", "ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vecq.comp"],
+      "anchors": ["GGML_ARIFI_ROCMFP4_MMVQ", "mul_mat_vec_rocmfp4_fast_q8_1_f32"],
+      "evidence": ["board/programs/local-inference/lanes/2026-09-02-lane-209-kernel-attacks-REPORT.md", "research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-09-02-lane-209/r10", "research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-09-02-lane-209/r8-integrate", "commit:f68a4bd25"],
+      "quality_gate": "THREE parts, and the third is the one that is still short. (1) test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT and -o MUL_MAT_ID on q4_0_rocmfp4_fast, 0 FAIL. (2) The lane-206 adversarial set: `test-backend-ops test -o MUL_MAT -p 'adv='` run twice, default env and GGML_VK_DISABLE_MMVQ=1, over byte-identical deterministic inputs - the arms MUST differ at exactly n=3 and n=5 and be identical at n=1/2/4, or MMVQ did not dispatch and the comparison is void. (3) Served: F-141 content floor 0/8, zero empty completions, and an ON-vs-ON control run alongside the ON-vs-OFF comparison, because without it a text difference cannot be attributed. Byte-identity is NOT the right bar for this mechanism - an int-dot path and an f32-dequant path cannot be bit-identical by construction - but a first-token EOG or an empty completion is a hard RED.",
+      "workload": "Radeon 780M gfx1103 Vulkan, julianmb Qwen3.8-27B-ROCmFP4-FAST 14.56 GB (99.54% q4_0_rocmfp4_fast, zero iq3_s and zero iq4_xs tensors, so it isolates this mechanism), seated DFlash2 Q4_K_M drafter at --spec-draft-n-max 2 so the target verify ubatch is n_draft+1 = 3, and a plain arm as control. Op ladder: test-backend-ops perf m=17408 k=5120 n=1,2,3,4,5,8.",
+      "measured_effect": "LANE-BINARY MEASUREMENT (engine-r4 -> engine-r10, epoch E2, matched 2x16 GB RAM): drafted decode 7.498 -> 9.518 mean t/s, +2.0199 [+1.3212, +2.7186], 8/8 cells positive = +26.9%; plain decode +0.0016 [-0.0168, +0.0199] tied; prefill tied; rolled quality 32/40 -> 33/40; zero empty completions across 64 rounds. Op ladder x1.356 at n=3 and x1.313 at n=5, with a GGML_VK_DISABLE_MMVQ=1 control flattening every row to x0.991-1.007, which is what attributes the gain to the port rather than to build drift.",
+      "valid_conditions": "AMD under Vulkan, on files carrying q4_0_rocmfp4_fast, at widths n=3 and n=5 ONLY - the same port is a LOSS above the gate and was measured so, and n=2 produced a deterministic first-token EOG in a served cache-history replay and is deliberately excluded. INERT, not broken, on the seated Huihui line, which carries no ROCmFP4 tensors. Ships default OFF pending independent clearance; the mechanism is unchanged by that and the env var takes it.",
+      "notes": "What is NOT yet established, and must not be quietly dropped by whoever clears this: n=5 has never executed in served generation, in lane-209 or in lane-206 - the seated n-max-2 line emits n=3 and never n=5, so the width is live in the selector and exercised only by test-backend-ops. Also, the lane-206 op gate found MMVQ CLOSER to the CPU reference than the f32 shader on every adversarial pattern; that is partly structural and must not be quoted as accuracy, because this type's CPU vec_dot_type is GGML_TYPE_Q8_0 (CHECKED ggml-cpu.c), so the reference is itself an int-quantized-activation path."
     }
   ]
 }
